# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Terra Calendar — environment configuration
#
# The FREE, open-source edition needs NONE of this. Leave it all unset (or omit
# the .env file entirely) and the app runs fully local — JSON file on desktop,
# local sync server / localStorage in the browser. No account, no server.
#
# Set the variables below ONLY for the PAID, hosted (cloud-synced) edition.
# Copy this file to ".env.local" and fill in your Supabase project values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# (VITE_BACKEND is retired — Cloud mode now activates at runtime for signed-in
#  users with an active subscription. Set the Supabase vars below to enable
#  accounts + Cloud.)

# From your Supabase project: Settings → API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-ref.supabase.co

# The PUBLISHABLE key (Settings → API Keys → "Publishable and secret API keys";
# starts with "sb_publishable_"). On older projects this is the legacy "anon"
# key instead. EITHER works here — both are SAFE to ship in the browser bundle,
# because access is enforced by Row-Level Security, not by hiding this key.
# NEVER put the "secret" / "service_role" key here — those bypass RLS.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxx

# Show in-app purchase buttons (Account section): the $3.99 cosmetics unlock and
# the Cloud subscription. Set to "true" ONLY after you've deployed the billing
# edge functions and created the Stripe products — see docs/BILLING_SETUP.md.
# Leave unset and the buttons stay hidden (entitlement status still displays).
VITE_BILLING_ENABLED=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Calendar sync (FREE, desktop edition) — OPTIONAL.
#
# Lets the desktop app sync with a user's own Google Calendar over CalDAV. It is
# independent of the Supabase settings above and needs no server we run.
#
# Create an OAuth client in Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials
# → "OAuth client ID" → application type "Desktop app", and enable the
# "Google Calendar API". The desktop flow uses PKCE (no client secret), so the
# client ID below is safe to ship in the bundle. Leave unset to hide the feature.
#
# For a PUBLIC/production build, bake the ID into DEFAULT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in
# src/data/google/googleConfig.ts (and publish + verify the consent screen — see
# docs/RELEASING.md) so it works for everyone without setting this var.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
